
==============================================================================
Feature selection and regularisation study
==============================================================================
train 31,120 rows | validation 7,780 rows | 775 features | imbalance 171.9:1

==============================================================================
1. Does the split matter? chronological vs shuffled
==============================================================================
  chronological split  PR-AUC 0.7312
  shuffled split       PR-AUC 0.7381
  inflation from shuffling: +0.0069

  The shuffled split puts the same cards and merchants on both sides of the
  boundary, so the model can memorise identities instead of learning fraud.
  That is why every number in this project comes from the time-based split.

